# The same policy as ../input.lg with the gates declared C, A, E, B, D and
# the cords shuffled. Verdicts and decision are unchanged (SPEC §7.5,
# rule 2). The §7.4 tie-break: C is declared first but not eligible until A
# is logged; A is logged first; then C, E and B are all eligible and are
# logged in declaration order C, E, B; D last. The log runs A, C, E, B, D
# (rule 3).
actor a
gate  C
gate  A grant a
gate  E grant a
gate  B grant a
gate  D grant a
cord C -> D
cord A -> E
cord a -> A
cord E -> D
cord A -> C
cord D -> master
cord B -> D
cord A -> B
